{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/181935-my-take-on-ctd-with-some-tweaks","id":181935,"title":"My take on CtD, with some tweaks.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-27T07:32:18-07:00","id":181935,"title":"My take on CtD, with some tweaks.","content":"I bought a paperback copy of CtD 1st ed corebook and browsed through it about three times when I had the opportunity. While I haven't been able to read it in depth fully (was able in certain parts). These are my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Likes.<br /> The artwork is pretty creative. And majority being in color is great as well as the few black n white pics.<br /> The self contain lore is awesome. Granted each has a brief overview, Changeling has theirs a bit more though out and the explanations fit per their universe.<br /> The Redcaps, Slaughs, and Trolls are some of my favorite Kiths. The others are pretty good, but they add that hint of darkness.<br /> The antagonists remind me of the Spectres from Wraith. The dark reflections of themselves that are not the Unseelie.<br /> How magic is set up is awesome. I like the combination possibilities and being able to pull it off on the fly. And the Bunk conditions are great prereqs.<br /> <br /> Changes I would make.<br /> The age range of the Seemings. Childer makes sense, but with Wilder and Grumps seems too young to me. Speaking of Seemings, not liking that its how &quot;old&quot; you are rather than what you are.<br /> While I like the card setup. I can see somebody stacking the deck so they can pull off 4 and/or 5 dot abilities with only 1 or 2 dot Bunks.<br /> The Eshu doesn't look very Changeling. While with the other Kiths does look the part, outside of their abilities the Eshu just looks more like regular mortals.<br /> The Unseelie should get a name change. While I can see the nobility using the term Unseelie as something to say in front of the people without trying to scare them. But when your down a dark alley and find something and realize that it's a (insert intimidating name here), you should change your underwear soon.<br /> I'm gonna skip my thing with Modern Fantasy. I'm pretty sure all the complaints have been heard so mines is probably going to be nothing new.<br /> Incorporating more technology. Not just having tech savy Changelings, but more high tech treasures and weapons. While some tech have been addressed but it seems more glossed over than fully fleshed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T18:27:50-07:00","id":182431,"title":"","content":"I would recommend you grab yourself a copy of Changeling Second Ed and then revisit this. The changes become quite distinct. I agree with you on many of these points though. I've always made NPCs older than the recommended age range. And Steampunk faeries FTW!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T02:25:28-07:00","id":182738,"title":"","content":"Oh wow. My friend, tell me, is Hansen still on the radio in your time machine? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like Darling says, pick up 2nd edition. it doesn't clean up EVERYTHING (Liam house boon, I'm looking at you!). Actually, Changeling's stuff is such a scattered mess, you might really want to work on filing the library before you go looking to make edits.I've had every changeling book for almost a decade now, and I'm still not sure what book contains what information I need - sometimes said information is 1st edition, sometimes it's 2nd edition, sometime it's that awkward teenage phase Changeling went through towards the end...<br /> <br /> To address your specific points though...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The artwork is pretty creative. And majority being in color is great as well as the few black n white pics </div> </div> </div>Funny, I found most of the art in 1st edition stuff to be kinda goddamned horrid.<br /> <img src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v181/Kittenpeeler/changelingart.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v181/Kittenpeeler/Cling.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> However, while i found the style <i>crude</i> i did sort of like that all the splat section art are characters from the immortal Eyes novel trilogy (though that Redcap doesn't seem very Edmund-ish to me...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The self contain lore is awesome. Granted each has a brief overview, Changeling has theirs a bit more though out and the explanations fit per their universe. </div> </div> </div>best thing about changeling lore, is that you can literally make it up as you go along. or you cna use what's there. or both. Great thing about nobody in the game actually having a clue about What Really Happened\u2122, instead piecing history together out of some common stuff kinda-remembered over various incarnations through the mists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Redcaps, Slaughs, and Trolls are some of my favorite Kiths. The others are pretty good, but they add that hint of darkness. </div> </div> </div>Oh, you can get darkness out of any of them. best thing is, the players never, ever, EVER suspect the seelie boggan to be involved in anything less than chaste and good...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How magic is set up is awesome. I like the combination possibilities and being able to pull it off on the fly. And the Bunk conditions are great prereqs. </div> </div> </div>2nd edition does away with pre-set bunks, instead allowing you to freeform them on the fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The age range of the Seemings. Childer makes sense, but with Wilder and Grumps seems too young to me. Speaking of Seemings, not liking that its how &quot;old&quot; you are rather than what you are. </div> </div> </div>It IS awkward... until you realize that really, the age ranges are supposed to be considered for <i>when the character awakens to their fae nature</i>. This is touched on in The enchanted - basically if your character starts out as a Childling, they don't immediately get shunted into Wilder when they turn thirteen; it's more dependent on their banality (of course, all those years of public school probably makes it match up pretty close) so you CAN easily have a 14 year old Childling, or a 25 year old Wilder, under certain conditions (especially when you measure in time spent in freeholds...) <b>BUT</b> a character who undergoes their chrysalis at age 15 or 26 is going to be a wilder or a grump, respectively; they've had ll the banality of a human tjeor age, but little if any of the glamour a changeling would have had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I like the card setup. I can see somebody stacking the deck so they can pull off 4 and/or 5 dot abilities with only 1 or 2 dot Bunks. </div> </div> </div>You would have liked it less back in the day this system was actually relevant - an eight-card booster pack cost two dollars and fifty cents, with over a hundred cards, all completely randomized... at $2.50 each. Dunno if you ever played magic, but back in 1994, $2.50 would have gotten you a 15-card booster pack with one guaranteed rare, AND you could use the cards themselves for a fun game. Changeling would break your bank for these dumb things and you couldn't do a damn thing with them besides this... though they seem to be premum collectors items these days, so hey, maybe they'd be worth the investment at the time.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition completely discards the card system. Hell, I think most of the 1st edition material ignores the hell out of it as well. More than anything, Changeling's initial reliance on peripherals - <i>expensive</i> peripherals that were clearly part of a fad-grab - is likely what doomed the game to one of the smallest of fan bases in the WoD systems.<br /> <br /> And then they came out with Arcadia: The Wyld Hunt... <i>Sigh</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Eshu doesn't look very Changeling. While with the other Kiths does look the part, outside of their abilities the Eshu just looks more like regular mortals. </div> </div> </div>Their differences are hardly so pronounced as being nine feet tll, horned, and blue yeah. But an Eshu calling on the Wyrd would still stand out in a crowd, what with their exotic attire, uncannily slender and long forms, and the whole &quot;hi, we have a galaxy in our eyeballs&quot; thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Unseelie should get a name change. While I can see the nobility using the term Unseelie as something to say in front of the people without trying to scare them. But when your down a dark alley and find something and realize that it's a (insert intimidating name here), you should change your underwear soon. </div> </div> </div>Seelie and Unseelie are not terms invented by Changeling. They're actually both Middle English terms, from the Scots-gaelic root word <i>seilie, </i>meaning &quot;luck / fortune / blessing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm gonna skip my thing with Modern Fantasy. I'm pretty sure all the complaints have been heard so mines is probably going to be nothing new.<br /> Incorporating more technology. Not just having tech savy Changelings, but more high tech treasures and weapons. While some tech have been addressed but it seems more glossed over than fully fleshed out. </div> </div> </div>Well, Treasures ultimately depend on the Dreaming.. .and the Dreaming, somewhat ironically, lags behind the modern world. it takes <i>time</i> for technological constructs and scientific conceits to become so widespread among humanity that they not only show up in the universe of dreams, but also work as intended. Chemical reactions don't work in the dreaming (Aside from fire and maybe some other simple things) because chemistry doesn't really <i>work</i> in dreams. it's mutable, just like everything else physics-derived.<br /> <br /> Now that said, the Nockers are able to overcome this with their Forge Chimera ability and some of the skills and Arts out of their kithbook... but they're pretty much alone in this (and of course whatever they make is flawed - Scientific Progress Goes &quot;Boink&quot; - and it's limited (gunpowder yes, NASA supercomputers, no... Hamster-powered babbage engines, maybe). if you want cutting-edge technology paired with sci fi / fantasy technobabble, you want Mage, three doors to the left, just follow the trail of lawn furniture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 06-28-2014, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T02:37:16-07:00","id":182745,"title":"","content":"damn I've always wanted to get into changeling... Mage has always taken my attention though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:59:33-07:00","id":182992,"title":"","content":"@ Darling_Rose: A friend of mine has a copy of second ed. He was going to lend it to me for a while until the bar we hung out at moved the dart board to a high traffic area. My local game store happen to have that (along with Street Fighter which I bought, and Wraith 1st ed but wasn't able to get that) and it was $8 (Street Fighter was $20). I'm going to try to revisit it but it's going to be a long while cause I want to save up the money first. Trust me, it took over 3 years to get all the core books for the 40k rpgs (couldn't find any used copies, all were full price).<br /> <br /> @ The Cat Came Back: Going through the points as I scroll.<br /> Art: Some of the Kiths aren't suppose to be good looking. Do you want a Redcap looking like Captain Wieniepants, or a Slaugh like Michelle Fifer? Me personally, no. If their suppose to make you cringe then cringe dammit!<br /> Lore: Cool. I'm going to have lots of fun with that.<br /> Seeming: That doesn't make more sense. Wouldn't you age? Hell, the book does say you can possibly age. But they only provide for starting age and not if you character ages naturally. Then what would be the difference between your age or the Seeming's age?<br /> My favs: Boggans don't have that potential for me. Satyrs and Pooka have more dark potential cause you might get a Pooka to lead you the wrong way or that Satyr is giving you &quot;the look&quot;. I see Boggans in a performance of The Ballard of Bilbo Baggins than horror.<br /> Magic (both): There was actual cards? That's cool and Oh God at the same time. Going to save the magic for the revisit. Another reason why I liked the cards is that everybody can have access to the magic without passing the book back and forth. One thing I was thinking about to punish deck stacking is that when the cantrip works, it's not as potent (vice versa with 1 or 2 dot combos with 4 or 5 Bunks).<br /> Eshu: Which none of that was featured in the book. About the only thing that suggested that the Eshu was other worldly was floating about six inches off the ground. The skin wasn't blue, No horns and if there were it was covered up by the headdress. And nobody standing next to him so couldn't tell how tall he is, just looking about average height.<br /> Unseelie name change: Makes sense. But to me Unseelie is more a name for nobility to use on something similar to &quot;Do not mention they that shall not be named!&quot; If you have a character going on a heelturn then they would try to track down the real name of the Unseelie faction.<br /> Changeling Tech: Going off of Darling_Rose's thing, I'd figure you can create some steampunky stuff. They also mention that you can chimera modern tech (the only example they had was chimera Harley Davisons). Got no problem with taking time since most tech would be promoting Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:10:31-07:00","id":183091,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE<br /> Art: Some of the Kiths aren't suppose to be good looking. Do you want a Redcap looking like Captain Wieniepants, or a Slaugh like Michelle Fifer? Me personally, no. If their suppose to make you cringe then cringe dammit![/quote]<br /> <br /> I was mostly talking about the QUALITY of the art. Here's the Redcap splat artwork from 2nd edition, for example:<br /> <img src=\"http://www.takissis.com/images/kith-redcap.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> 1st editions tend to have pretty... odd art. Ever seen 1st edition Werewolf? Oh my lord, it's like FurCon...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seeming: That doesn't make more sense. Wouldn't you age? Hell, the book does say you can possibly age. But they only provide for starting age and not if you character ages naturally. Then what would be the difference between your age or the Seeming's age? </div> </div> </div>Well, it's kind of a confusing thing. Seeming is dependant both on banality AND age, but seems to rely more on banality; a childling who catches a third permanant Banality is more likely to slide into early Wilderhood, than a Banality 1 Childling is to become a wilder right smack on their 13th birthday. It's basically wibbly-wobbly timey-wimey stuff<br /> <br /> But the &quot;hard&quot; ages are assuming your character <i>just</i> had their chrysalis not too long ago, coming out of hte mortal world into that of the changelings very recently. As a mortal, you weren't able to avoid banality through use of glamour or questing or oaths, so you've got that baggage on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My favs: Boggans don't have that potential for me. Satyrs and Pooka have more dark potential cause you might get a Pooka to lead you the wrong way or that Satyr is giving you &quot;the look&quot;. I see Boggans in a performance of The Ballard of Bilbo Baggins than horror. </div> </div> </div>Think Varys, from Game of Thrones.<br /> <br /> Lots of freeholds are run by boggans. THose that aren't, usually have Boggans as stewards. And cooks. or whatever. What noble's entourage lacks a boggan to act as seneschal, or to take care of the wardrobe? Boggans are everywhere. They see and hear everything. They're ingratiated up and down the social strata of the kithain, from the powdered and primped Boggan herald at king David's court to the one-armed fry cook down at the local unseelie mew. Everyone's their friends, because boggans are so helpful, and so harmless! What proud troll wouldn't stand as champion for some hapless boggan being accused of something untoward? Even if he doesn't LIKE the boggan, odds are he <i>owes</i> the Boggan for something, down the line. Boggans gossip constantly, among themselves; what one boggan knows, thirty others will find out before the week is out... and they keep it to themselves. They ca see who the movers and shakers are in a given scenario, at just a glance.<br /> <br /> Boggans are <i>great</i> for antagonists centered in spiderwebs of intrigue, obligation, and rumor. No, they're not great to use as up-front, sword-in-your-face antagonists... But the look on your players' faces when they realize they've been getting played all along by the tubby little tailor who wanted revenge against the local Eiluned, and more <i>that they can't touch him</i>? That's gold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magic (both): There was actual cards? That's cool and Oh God at the same time. Going to save the magic for the revisit. Another reason why I liked the cards is that everybody can have access to the magic without passing the book back and forth. One thing I was thinking about to punish deck stacking is that when the cantrip works, it's not as potent (vice versa with 1 or 2 dot combos with 4 or 5 Bunks). </div> </div> </div>Well, if you like the mechanic, use it. I've always been a little curious about how it actually works out, myself, and i'd like to hear about it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eshu: Which none of that was featured in the book. About the only thing that suggested that the Eshu was other worldly was floating about six inches off the ground. The skin wasn't blue, No horns and if there were it was covered up by the headdress. And nobody standing next to him so couldn't tell how tall he is, just looking about average height. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I told you the splat art wasn't great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Tony DiTerlizzi's interpretation of the kith (Page 82, the splash for the third chapter of 1st edition) does more justice. But no, they're simply not the most outlandish-looking of the kiths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unseelie name change: Makes sense. But to me Unseelie is more a name for nobility to use on something similar to &quot;Do not mention they that shall not be named!&quot; If you have a character going on a heelturn then they would try to track down the real name of the Unseelie faction. </div> </div> </div>Well, Seelie and Unseelie aren't really &quot;factions&quot; - they're not like, say, Tradition vs. Technocracy, or Camarilla vs. Sabbat. Think of it more as a loose definition of an individual based on their personality. And when i say &quot;loose,&quot; I mean just that - unless a character goes around espousing the Seelie or Unseelie codes, <i>you don't know</i> - and even then he could just be lying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changeling Tech: Going off of Darling_Rose's thing, I'd figure you can create some steampunky stuff. They also mention that you can chimera modern tech (the only example they had was chimera Harley Davisons). Got no problem with taking time since most tech would be promoting Banality. </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, Nockers have greatly advanced steam technology. Judging from the kith book, they're also <i>starting</i> to get their paws on Tesla-style electrical stuff... like you know, death rays.<br /> <br /> Note that <i>technology</i> doesn't promote banality... but letting technology take over for your brain <i>does</i>. Television for instance, isn't banal - hell, the Resurgence only happened <i>because</i> of television! But the dude who slumps on his couch and watches the screen for eight hours a day, and doesn't talk about anything besides star trek or DBZ? he's banal as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:44:16-07:00","id":183113,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/181935-my-take-on-ctd-with-some-tweaks?p=183091#post183091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u2026and doesn't talk about anything besides star trek or DBZ? he's banal as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, his Banality would be\u2026<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">OVER 9000!!</span></span></b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:47:36-07:00","id":183160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/181935-my-take-on-ctd-with-some-tweaks?p=183091#post183091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think Varys, from Game of Thrones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it myself, another great example/inspiration would be Gideon Gleeful from the Disney animated show, Gravity Falls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the dude who slumps on his couch and watches the screen for eight hours a day, and doesn't talk about anything besides star trek or DBZ? he's banal as hell. </div> </div> </div>But what if he writes fanfiction or does fanart for those shows then? Seeing as how fanfiction has been compared to the method of storytelling the Greeks did with their mythic heroes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T13:23:42-07:00","id":183185,"title":"","content":"Also, Seelie isn't &quot;good&quot; and Unseelie isn't &quot;evil&quot; and any Changeling can switch between which court is dominant in themselves. The Sidhe tend to do this more often than the commoners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T18:15:35-07:00","id":183404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/181935-my-take-on-ctd-with-some-tweaks?p=182992#post182992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Darling_Rose: A friend of mine has a copy of second ed. He was going to lend it to me for a while until the bar we hung out at moved the dart board to a high traffic area. My local game store happen to have that (along with Street Fighter which I bought, and Wraith 1st ed but wasn't able to get that) and it was $8 (Street Fighter was $20). I'm going to try to revisit it but it's going to be a long while cause I want to save up the money first. Trust me, it took over 3 years to get all the core books for the 40k rpgs (couldn't find any used copies, all were full price).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So your friend will only let you borrow the Changeling core book as long as it's in some nice quiet area for you to read it without letting you take it home? Some friend. And 8$ is too much for you? Are you 12? No more allowance money to afford a book that's 8$ and 20$ streetfighter at the same time? There's a 25$ high rez PDF version from Drive thru RPG. <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1624/Changeling-the-Dreaming-2nd-Edition?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...d-Edition?it=1</a><br /> <br /> If that doesn't work for you check out Amazon<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://amzn.com/1565047168\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://amzn.com/1565047168\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://amzn.com/1565047168\" target=\"_blank\"> http://amzn.com/1565047168 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or save a search on Ebay so that it emails you whenever a Changeling the Dreaming corebook is listed. Sometimes they're only 5$.<br /> <br /> And if you wanna bid on some Cantrip cards, try here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://r.ebay.com/N8jJuM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://r.ebay.com/N8jJuM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://r.ebay.com/N8jJuM\" target=\"_blank\"> http://r.ebay.com/N8jJuM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/181935-my-take-on-ctd-with-some-tweaks?p=182992#post182992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favs: Boggans don't have that potential for me. Satyrs and Pooka have more dark potential cause you might get a Pooka to lead you the wrong way or that Satyr is giving you &quot;the look&quot;. I see Boggans in a performance of The Ballard of Bilbo Baggins than horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the others. There's horror there if you dare to look for it. Unseelie Boggans are known as Boggarts and Boogeymen. The kind of fae that don't seem all that threatening because they look so nice, but then you're supposed to look trustworthy until they trick you into a trap. When Satyrs go deeply Unseelie they can let their passions run wild. Rapist is probably only the tip of the iceberg. No dark Pooka? Clearly you've never encountered a lobster or cockroach Pooka. Or one that's based off a boar or warthog. Snake, Spider, even a Bumblebee. Why think they all have to be cute?<br /> <br /> On technology being Banal, why believe that either? Technology is invented through a very creative process. New discoveries, new ways of doing things, countless possibilities for the future of a new gadget. That's Glamour right there. What is done with that technology, that's where Banality comes in. TV is a really good example of creativity. And yeah spending 8 hours sitting on the couch, that can be banal, writing loads of fan fiction during or drawing fan art, then that would not be Banal. Yet again it's all up to the individual. It's not the Activity that is Banal specifically, it is what that person does that determines what has Glamour and what is Banal. Sort of the opposite with Seelie and Unseelie. It's not the fae themselves, but what they Do that makes them Seelie or Unseelie. Not &quot;Good&quot; or &quot;Evil&quot;. More like Generous and empathetic, vs. Selfish and self-centered. The Seelie thinking of others and what is good for the realm and the Dreamers that sustain them, Vs the Unseelie who think the world owes them a living, Dreamers are theirs to use and discard and getting power over others is their main goal. As a glance they don't outwardly seem any different. It's how they act that's the key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T03:46:47-07:00","id":183684,"title":"","content":"No. But I work at Walmart so the pay is pretty much the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T07:07:25-07:00","id":183765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/181935-my-take-on-ctd-with-some-tweaks?p=183684#post183684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. But I work at Walmart so the pay is pretty much the same.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then Amazon and Ebay are gonna be your best bet for finding core books on a budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}